        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Steam is now rolling out age verification in Australia for R18+ games, and the method Valve chose is already getting a lot of people annoyed.\n\nThe system asks users to add a credit card to prove they’re 18 or older and people don’t have a credit card and normally use debit cards instead.\n\nCertain debit cards actually work and others not depending on the bank, which makes the whole system even more confusing. \n\nAnd there’s another issue, people say they can be blocked from even viewing the store page for games they already own, including games like Cyberpunk 2077. \n\nI understand that Valve need to follow Australia’s new age-verification rules, but making a credit card the main way to prove you’re an adult when for some people their account is over 18 years old feels unnecessary"
        },
